// ## 6. Findings summary (by severity)

// CRITICAL (1):
//   C1. oodac/check/smt/ missing. RFC-0002 (design-by-contract) is
//       marked Status: Implemented in openOODA/rfcs/0002-design-by-
//       contract.oot, but the SMT verifier harness directory is not
//       on disk. governance_verify FAILs on this. Lock evidence gap.
//       Owner: compiler lane (muse/oodac). RULES §1.5, §1.7.

// MAJOR (4):
//   M1. 3 files exceed the 256-line cap (RULES §1.8):
//       oodac/.github/workflows/ci.yml:280,
//       oodac/tests/fixtures/boundary_257_lines.oo:257,
//       oodar/CHANGES.md:1745.
//       The boundary_257 fixture is itself a test of the 257-line
//       boundary; arguably out of scope, but governance_enforce FAILs.
//   M2. 2 .oo files lack the 4-element Academy header (RULES §1.11):
//       ooda/fix/text.oo, oodac/qa/scratch_lineno.oo.
//   M3. INDEX.oot (2026-09-09) snapshot is 1-12 tags stale across all
//       12 product repos. The snapshot column is not a SSoT (per
//       RULES §1.24 it must be derived from git history) but the
//       file presents it as one. Drift finding, not a code defect.
//   M4. moonshot_scorecard.oot:21 claims "oodar/qa/ has 22
//       challenger_*.c"; the polyrepo has 0 challenger_*.c files.
//       Stale claim.

// MINOR (4):
//   m1. 6 dirty files in oodac, 1 in install at audit time. Not
//       blockers; record for transparency.
//   m2. .github/ last commit is 2026-09-07 (3 days stale). Org
//       profile; not blocking, but visible.
//   m3. 11 of 12 product repos have no AGENT.md / AGENTS.oot
//       (only openOODA, .github do). RULES does not require
//       per-repo AGENT files, but most repos do not document
//       their agent-facing contract.
//   m4. moonshot_scorecard.oot dated 2026-09-09; 1 day stale.
//       Today (2026-09-10) the scorecard is 6.0/10 (re-derived).

// NOTE (3):
//   n1. Host-compiled lock execution path is broken: `oodac build
//       openOODA/scripts/proof_of_today.oo` emits LLVM IR but fails
//       at the `print` call ("unknown call print"). The audit fell
//       back to re-running each lock's embedded shell directly. This
//       is itself a release-blocker for the moonshot because the
//       locks cannot be invoked end-to-end on the host toolchain.
//   n2. The user-profile enumeration of 9 process boards is stale.
//       The 2026-09-02 governance refactor (NORTHSTAR.oot:14)
//       consolidated to 3 onboarding + 7 RFCs + 3 practices = 13.
//       This is by design; the audit surfaces it for transparency.
//   n3. 4 files in the org are 256+ lines (above) and SHIPPED.oot is
//       not on disk anywhere in the polyrepo. RULES §1.8 expects
//       256-line cap to apply uniformly. The on-disk truth is
//       that SHIPPED.oot has been superseded; INDEX.oot is the new
//       release SSoT. This is a refactor outcome, not a defect.

